    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d423">

                <pb facs="0536" n="452" sameAs="frus:frus1903/pg452"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr. White.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-12-05"><hi rendition="#italic">December 5,
                        1902</hi>.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Hay states that, at the request of J. and W. Seligman &amp; Co., bankers,
                    New York, who are trying to make an arrangement to effect a settlement of the
                    Venezuelan debt, it gives him pleasure to say that the President would be glad
                    if such, an arrangement could be made as might obviate the necessity of any
                    exhibition of force on the part of Germany and Great Britain. Mr. White will
                    understand, however, that the United States Government assumes no obligation
                    whatever in the nature either of a material or moral guaranty of any liabilities
                    created by the transaction.</p>
                <p>This instruction is sent for Mr. White’s information in case anyone in interest
                    makes inquiry of him.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
